  "reason": "Evidence: config_038 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile + transformer + concat) achieved the best validation accuracy (0.7207), a clear jump over the best RNA-only result (0.6530). However, the fusion strategy has never been varied in any completed experiment—concat is the only fusion tested. Question: config_039 is identical to config_038 except fusion changes from concat to weighted, isolating the effect of the fusion mechanism while holding all other design choices (encoder, profile, aggregation, image encoder) at their best-evidenced settings. Why this is the best next experiment: it is a clean single-variable comparison that directly exploits the strongest evidence while reducing uncertainty about a completely untested design axis. If weighted fusion improves on concat, it reveals a new optimization direction; if it is comparable or worse, we can confidently fix fusion=concat and redirect budget toward other untested dimensions (e.g., aggregation in multimodal or image encoder choice). Under a limited budget, this targeted test is more informative than simultaneously changing multiple variables or revisiting dimensions already well-characterized (e.g., transformer vs avgpool, which showed a negligible gap in RNA-only)."
}

